{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/system()"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"],"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@attached"},{"kind":"text","text":"(extension, conformances: "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems6SystemP","text":"System","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems15MainActorSystemP","text":"MainActorSystem","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"},{"kind":"text","text":", names: named(access), named(run), named(initialize)) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Attach ","type":"text"},{"code":"@System","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to a structure with a method named ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The method’s parameters are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system parameters, values the schedule fetches from the world before each run, and their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"types state exactly what the system reads and writes. The macro conforms the type to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", writing its ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" from those types and a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fetches the parameters and calls your method.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following system moves each entity by its velocity plus whichever of a wind and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"current act on it, scaled by the time step:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct Wind: Component { var speed: Double }","struct Current: Component { var speed: Double }","","@System","struct Drift {","    func run(","        _ drifters: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity, AnyOf<Wind, Current>>,","        _ step: ResourceReader<TimeStep>","    ) {","        drifters { position, row in","            let (velocity, (wind, current)) = row.components","            let push = (wind?.speed ?? 0) + (current?.speed ?? 0)","            position.x += (velocity.dx + push) * step.value.seconds","        }","    }","}","","var world = World()","world.resources.insert(TimeStep(seconds: 0.5))","let boat = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 2, dy: 0), Wind(speed: 4))","Schedule { Drift() }.run(on: &world)","print(world[Position.self, of: boat].x)","\/\/ Prints \"3.0\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Drift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes ","type":"text"},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", reads ","type":"text"},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Wind","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Current","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"TimeStep","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" resource,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and nothing else, so a schedule runs it at the same time as any system that doesn’t write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"those types.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"These are the parameter types a ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method can take:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"definition":{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reads components.","type":"text"}]}]},"term":{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query\/Where","isActive":true}]}},{"definition":{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Writes components, optionally reading others.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},"term":{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}},{"definition":{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read or write a resource."}]}]},"term":{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}},{"definition":{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read or send events."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},"term":{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","isActive":true}]}},{"definition":{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lists the entities that lost a component."}]}]},"term":{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}},{"definition":{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Queues structural changes, which apply at the end of the system’s wave and conflict with nothing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},"term":{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands","isActive":true}]}}],"type":"termList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method that takes the world instead, as "},{"code":"inout World","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", makes a system with no access,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which can change anything and so runs alone:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@System","struct SpawnBall {","    func run(in world: inout World) {","        world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 0, dy: 0))","    }","}","","var world = World()","Schedule { SpawnBall() }.run(on: &world)","print(world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"1\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Mark the type or its ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method ","type":"text"},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to make a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem","type":"reference"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The macro reads only the method’s signature. Two parameters whose written types conflict,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"such as an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Update<Position>"},{"text":" and a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Query<Position>"},{"text":", are a compile-time error. A conflict